<section>

  <h2>1. Executive Overview</h2>

  <p>

    Jeremy Blueprint presents a vision for an interconnected

    artificial intelligence companion designed around

    human needs, independence and long-term wellbeing.

  </p>

  <p>

    Rather than treating artificial intelligence as an

    isolated chatbot, the framework proposes a connected

    ecosystem capable of supporting people throughout

    everyday life.

  </p>

  <p>

    Its guiding principle is that intelligence should

    serve humanity, not require humanity to adapt to it.

  </p>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>2. Origins and Development</h2>

  <p>

    The concept developed through earlier explorations

    known as Buddy and Jeremy in a Bottle during

    early 2025.

  </p>

  <p>

    It subsequently evolved into Jeremy Blueprint,

    a broader human-first artificial intelligence vision.

  </p>

  <p>

    The creator maintains historical development records

    and correspondence relating to the concept.

    Independent verification of the complete development

    chronology has not been published here.

  </p>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>3. The Human-First Principles</h2>

  <ul>

    <li>Human independence and autonomy</li>

    <li>Safeguarding and proactive protection</li>

    <li>Privacy and user-controlled information</li>

    <li>Accessibility and inclusion</li>

    <li>Transparency and accountability</li>

    <li>Personal growth and opportunity</li>

    <li>Responsible companionship</li>

  </ul>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>4. The Proposed Companion Ecosystem</h2>

  <p>

    Jeremy Blueprint proposes connected support across

    multiple areas of human life.

  </p>

  <ul>

    <li>Safety, safeguarding and emergency assistance</li>

    <li>Organisation, memory and daily planning</li>

    <li>Wellbeing and responsible companionship</li>

    <li>Learning, careers and personal development</li>

    <li>Accessibility and independent living</li>

    <li>Financial and legal information navigation</li>

    <li>Healthcare and public-service navigation</li>

    <li>Community and social connection</li>

    <li>Transport, devices and future robotics integration</li>

    <li>News, alerts and contextual information</li>

  </ul>

  <p>

    These are proposed capabilities rather than

    claims of a fully implemented product.

  </p>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>5. Safeguarding and Human Independence</h2>

  <p>

    The framework places human safety and independent

    decision-making at the centre of AI companionship.

  </p>

  <p>

    Proposed safeguards include proactive risk awareness,

    emergency assistance, appropriate human oversight

    and clear boundaries for sensitive situations.

  </p>

  <p>

    Any real-world implementation would require

    technical validation, privacy safeguards,

    appropriate professional oversight and

    compliance with applicable law.

  </p>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>6. Personal Memory and Continuity</h2>

  <p>

    Jeremy Blueprint envisions a companion that can

    support long-term goals, personal organisation

    and continuity across everyday activities.

  </p>

  <p>

    Users should remain informed about what information

    is retained and have meaningful control over

    personal information.

  </p>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>7. Accessibility and Inclusion</h2>

  <p>

    The vision includes support for people with

    different abilities, circumstances and

    accessibility requirements.

  </p>

  <p>

    The objective is to expand independence and

    access to opportunity rather than create

    unnecessary dependence on technology.

  </p>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>8. Research and Development Priorities</h2>

  <ul>

    <li>Privacy-preserving personal memory</li>

    <li>Safeguarding and emergency-response validation</li>

    <li>Human oversight and professional boundaries</li>

    <li>Accessibility and inclusive interface design</li>

    <li>Secure interoperability with external services</li>

    <li>Long-term wellbeing and autonomy evaluation</li>

    <li>Technical feasibility and prototype development</li>

  </ul>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>9. Current Development Status</h2>

  <p>

    Jeremy Blueprint is an independently documented

    conceptual framework and proposed ecosystem.

  </p>

  <p>

    This publication does not claim a deployed,

    commercially validated AI platform or a

    completed technical implementation.

  </p>

  <p>

    Future progress would require engineering,

    research, safety testing, partnerships and

    independent evaluation.

  </p>

</section>

